{"question": "when did nigeria become a federation of 19 states", "final_text": "Based on my knowledge, I can answer this question:\n\nNigeria became a federation of 19 states on **August 27, 1996** (with the creation process completed in November 1996). This significant constitutional amendment was implemented under the military government of General Ibrahim Badamasi Babangida. The restructuring created 6 new states which, when added to the existing 13 states, brought the total to 19 states, plus the Federal Capital Territory (Abuja) which had separate status.\n\nThe 6 new states created were:\n1. Anambra\n2. Delta\n3. Ebonyi\n4. Enugu\n5. Gombe\n6. Jigawa\n\nThis restructuring was approved by the Supreme Military Council and came into effect between late August and November 1996.\n\n<answer>1996 (specifically August 27, 1996, with implementation completed in November 1996)</answer><|im_end|>", "answer": "1996 (specifically August 27, 1996, with implementation completed in November 1996)", "exact_match": false, "reward": 0.2, "native_websearch_calls": 2, "tool_errors": 2, "cc_exit_code": 0, "elapsed_s": 8.964911733055487, "sampling_parameters": {"temperature": 1.0, "top_p": 1.0, "top_k": -1, "max_new_tokens": 2048, "stop": null, "stop_token_ids": [248046, 248044], "skip_special_tokens": false, "no_stop_trim": true, "spaces_between_special_tokens": false}, "model": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B", "segments": 1, "trainable_tokens": 516}
